From 9dd3e538cf51c8f71b2e1fb45058e67c58f1ddda Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nerves TickWatch Pro 3 <nerves@example.invalid>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] build: use bundled kernel headers by default

strace 7.0 predates the io_uring UAPI shipped by Linux 7.1.  Its version
check still chooses the target sysroot headers, then the io_uring decoder
fails a compile-time layout assertion.  Use strace's bundled, matching UAPI
definitions unless the caller explicitly selects another mode.

---
 configure | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/configure b/configure
index c68fb82..2f5f53e 100755
--- a/configure
+++ b/configure
@@ -6635,7 +6635,7 @@ Valid options are: yes, no, check.
 		;;
 	 esac
 else case e in #(
-  e) enable_bundled=check
+  e) enable_bundled=yes
  ;;
 esac
 fi
-- 
